WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:01.876
This is real wasabi.

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:03.128
Joe: Oh, it's, like, thick.

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:04.462
Whoa!

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:05.964
Hotter than — oh, s---.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.676
It's really spicy, Yuelei.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.844
Oh, but it's good.

00:00:12.887 --> 00:00:14.305
[coughs]

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:16.975
And these are wasabi-flavored.

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.019
Holy s---, these are hot.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.186
Holy s---.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.688
Welcome to "Flavor Binge."

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.274
If you're just here for the binge,

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:25.483
you can skip to the next chapter.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.653
But stick around to find
out what wasabi actually is.

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:31.072
Doesn't, does not smell

00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:32.449
spicy at all, yeah.

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:35.076
Has a bit of, like, a carrot vibe to it.

00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:35.910
Smells nice.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.704
Smells like the stuff you're
used to seeing with your sushi,

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.955
but maybe a little bit sweeter.

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:41.207
Raw wasab.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.294
Yep, I'm definitely tasting it.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:45.128
Ooh.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.171
But

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.424
that's not how you make wasabi, guys.

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:50.258
Without a grater,

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:52.135
you can't break the cells down properly,

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:53.678
and therefore you're not
releasing all the chemicals

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:55.263
to get all of the flavor out of it.

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:57.599
Wasabi stores two molecules
in two separate compartments,

00:00:57.599 --> 00:00:59.893
which mix when the plant is
broken down to activate them,

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.561
kind of like snapping a glow stick.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.480
I don't know if I can
get a paste off of this,

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.481
but I'll try.

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:13.031
[laughs]

00:01:14.616 --> 00:01:15.658
Yeah.

00:01:15.658 --> 00:01:17.202
Whoa.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.245
It's significantly hotter.

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:22.832
Whoo!

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:24.000
But there's a problem.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.544
Most of the products you buy
advertised as wasabi flavor

00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:28.713
actually contain little,
or even no wasabi.

00:01:28.713 --> 00:01:30.340
Some experts have even estimated

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.093
that 99% of the wasabi eaten by Americans

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.260
is actually fake.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.595
There's two main reasons for that.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.139
One of them you'll have
to wait 30 minutes for.

00:01:38.139 --> 00:01:39.766
But the other we'll tell you now.

00:01:41.726 --> 00:01:44.145
Real wasabi is very expensive.

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:48.149
A kilogram of fresh wasabi
can cost up to 250 bucks.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:50.485
This little piece right here is

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.279
52 grams.

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:55.448
What is —

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.659
so, wait, how much is that?

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:00.328
This is mostly due to
how hard it is to grow.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.914
Wasabi is a super-needy plant.

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:05.375
It can be killed by the slightest change

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:06.918
in temperature or sunlight.

00:02:06.918 --> 00:02:07.752
Same.

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:09.254
So what do food producers do instead?

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.297
Well, they tend to use horseradish.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.299
It's a plant from the
same family as wasabi

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:16.136
with plenty of allyl isothiocyanate.

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:18.054
I've never seen one in person before.

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:20.098
And it looks kind of like a really thick

00:02:20.098 --> 00:02:21.808
wizard's wand.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.935
I'm not gonna say the other
thing it looks like on camera.

00:02:23.935 --> 00:02:25.979
Horseradish is way cheaper than wasabi.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.481
This 200-gram piece cost me £1.85,

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.900
or about $2.45.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:34.404
The same amount of wasabi
would cost you $50.

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:36.406
This is the smallest piece they had.

00:02:36.406 --> 00:02:37.365
Look at this.

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:39.075
Look how big,

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:40.952
ugh, this thing of horseradish is.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:45.623
It's like a leg of a baby grand piano.

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:46.875
Let's put it to the test ourselves

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:49.002
and make our own fake wasabi.

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:51.045
It does smell pretty
similar to the wasabi did

00:02:51.045 --> 00:02:52.046
when I chopped that.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:55.216
Oh, I felt that.

00:02:57.927 --> 00:02:58.928
Do we have a hammer?

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:00.763
Oh, there we go.

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:05.351
It's hard to get a firm grasp on.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.228
[crew laughing]

00:03:07.228 --> 00:03:08.938
Stop it. [laughs]

00:03:11.149 --> 00:03:11.983
All right.

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:14.277
Rest of this goes right in the trash.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:17.947
Then we'll add a little bit of mustard.

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:21.201
A couple drops, right?

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:23.578
You think that was too much?

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:24.746
What do you think?

00:03:24.746 --> 00:03:26.581
Little too green?

00:03:26.581 --> 00:03:28.917
So, here is my homemade fake wasabi.

00:03:30.084 --> 00:03:31.628
And it does kind of smell like wasabi.

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:35.215
That's exact — oof.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.883
Ooh, I can feel it in my nostrils.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.468
That's exactly what I would expect.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.804
In both the US and the UK,

00:03:41.804 --> 00:03:44.265
you can get a range of wasabi
powders and wasabi pastes,

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:46.517
but with varying amounts
of actual wasabi in them.

00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:47.727
Don't know what we're gonna do with

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.938
a kilogram of 2% wasabi powder

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.356
after this shoot, but.

00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:54.025
The only 100% pure wasabi
powder I could find in the UK

00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:55.985
was from a website called JustIngredients.

00:03:55.985 --> 00:03:58.363
But it cost £844 per kilogram,

00:03:58.363 --> 00:04:00.073
so we've decided not to buy that one.

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:04.035
This gigantic bag seems
to have zero real wasabi

00:04:04.035 --> 00:04:05.745
and only has horseradish and mustard

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:08.122
listed on the label as flavorings.

00:04:08.122 --> 00:04:09.457
Ugh.

00:04:09.457 --> 00:04:11.960
Woof, it doesn't smell like wasabi.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.086
Yeah, already a much different,

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.796
a much more pleasant odor.

00:04:14.796 --> 00:04:15.672
And just look at the pot.

00:04:15.672 --> 00:04:18.424
You can totally visually
tell the difference, right?

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.218
The hundy. Oh, yeah.

00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:21.427
This, whoa.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.595
It actually smells pretty nice.

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:35.984
That's got the strongest taste
of anything I've had so far.

00:04:38.027 --> 00:04:38.861
Yeah.

00:04:40.405 --> 00:04:41.239
Whoa!

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:45.243
Whoa. 100%?

00:04:46.869 --> 00:04:49.497
About as spicy. It was a lot earthier.

00:04:49.497 --> 00:04:51.749
Look how happy this guy
is. Look at this guy.

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.795
He's just thrilled.

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.879
He's thrilled to be here.

00:04:56.879 --> 00:04:58.214
We all are.

00:04:58.214 --> 00:04:59.424
We'll start with this one from S&amp;B,

00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:02.093
which contains just 4.5% real wasabi.

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:12.312
That's enough wasabi. Oh, man.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.938
Joe: So, this is the real wasabi.

00:05:13.938 --> 00:05:15.064
Oh, it's, like, thick.

00:05:15.064 --> 00:05:16.232
Look at that. Look how thick this is.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:20.737
Whoa!

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:22.238
Hotter than — oh, s---.

00:05:26.117 --> 00:05:28.578
It's really spicy, Yuelei.

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:30.288
