Itsu crispy seaweed thins.

00:11:57.049 --> 00:11:59.218
Itsu is a chain in the
UK that does Asian food.

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.226
That was pretty good.

00:12:07.226 --> 00:12:10.479
Wasabi — aw, look how un-fun this is.

00:12:13.774 --> 00:12:14.900
Ugh!

00:12:19.447 --> 00:12:21.657
It's the seaweed part
that I hate, to be honest.

00:12:21.657 --> 00:12:23.826
Next up we've got these
Ocean's Halo seaweed thins.

00:12:23.826 --> 00:12:25.953
I mean, they look identical
to the previous ones.

00:12:34.128 --> 00:12:36.630
These are very salty, but
I get almost no wasabi,

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.299
especially compared to the Itsu one.

00:12:38.299 --> 00:12:40.092
Why are we doing this?

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:42.762
Is this ... ?

00:12:43.637 --> 00:12:45.181
Why are we eating seaweed?

00:12:50.853 --> 00:12:51.771
I don't know.

00:12:51.771 --> 00:12:53.606
Nope, as bad as the other one.

00:12:53.606 --> 00:12:55.733
Then finally we got some
Marks &amp; Spencer seaweed thins.

00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:00.279
I think these are the most wasabi

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:01.822
of the ones that I've tried.

00:13:01.822 --> 00:13:03.449
Probably second place to those.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:04.950
Last place to those.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.411
Korean. Seaweed snack. Wasabi.

00:13:11.791 --> 00:13:13.834
All the seaweed was trash.

00:13:13.834 --> 00:13:14.835
Then we're onto some crackers.

00:13:14.835 --> 00:13:15.836
It's another Itsu offering.

00:13:15.836 --> 00:13:18.172
These ones are prawn
crackers with mild wasabi.

00:13:19.423 --> 00:13:21.759
I get a very small amount of wasabi.

00:13:21.759 --> 00:13:23.135
Honestly, I don't think it's

00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:24.762
a worthwhile addition to a prawn cracker.

00:13:24.762 --> 00:13:26.472
I think they're already
tasty enough as they are.

00:13:30.309 --> 00:13:31.685
The first thing I tasted was wasabi,

00:13:31.685 --> 00:13:33.395
but that did disappear pretty quickly,

00:13:33.395 --> 00:13:35.105
and then it's just kind of
nice sweet rice cracker.

00:13:35.105 --> 00:13:35.940
Not bad.

00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:39.527
Gimme something fun.

00:13:39.527 --> 00:13:43.322
Get this horrible seaweed
taste out of my mouth.

00:13:43.322 --> 00:13:44.240
Ooh!

00:13:46.575 --> 00:13:47.409
Yeah.

00:13:48.953 --> 00:13:49.954
There's a lot —

00:13:50.996 --> 00:13:53.249
holy s---, these are hot.

00:13:53.249 --> 00:13:54.583
Holy s---.

00:13:54.583 --> 00:13:56.377
Oh! Oh!

00:13:56.377 --> 00:13:57.670
I can't have a second one.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:58.546
Oh!

00:14:00.923 --> 00:14:01.757
Ah!

00:14:03.217 --> 00:14:05.761
Leon: I think

00:14:05.761 --> 00:14:07.805
you don't get to choose
how much goes on these.

00:14:07.805 --> 00:14:08.639
Harry: Oh, God.

00:14:08.639 --> 00:14:09.974
Leon: I think we get to choose.

00:14:09.974 --> 00:14:12.017
Harry: Oh, no. I don't
want to. I don't like this.

00:14:12.017 --> 00:14:13.435
That's far too much!

00:14:13.435 --> 00:14:15.062
Are you insane?

00:14:15.062 --> 00:14:16.105
Feel like this is revenge

00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:18.732
for how difficult I am to work with.

00:14:18.732 --> 00:14:21.277
I hate everything about this.

00:14:21.277 --> 00:14:22.444
First up,

00:14:22.444 --> 00:14:26.490
fat-free wasabi Dijon dressing.

00:14:29.243 --> 00:14:30.077
Ugh.

00:14:30.077 --> 00:14:32.580
Yes, this cracker's been marinating

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.664
in the sauce.

00:14:38.085 --> 00:14:39.128
Nope.

00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:42.673
Well, I can barely taste wasabi.

00:14:42.673 --> 00:14:43.507
Oh, there it is.

00:14:48.679 --> 00:14:50.222
It's obviously got the texture of mayo

00:14:50.222 --> 00:14:51.974
and the kind of creaminess,
but then does still have

00:14:51.974 --> 00:14:54.101
a fairly strong wasabi
taste coming through.

00:14:55.352 --> 00:14:56.770
Not two things your brain kind of

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.273
expects to be associated with each other.

00:14:59.273 --> 00:15:00.941
For real?

00:15:00.941 --> 00:15:01.859
This much?

00:15:08.657 --> 00:15:09.742
That's just, like, more mayo

00:15:09.742 --> 00:15:11.785
than I want to put in
my mouth at one time.

00:15:12.703 --> 00:15:14.663
Wasabi mustard.

00:15:14.663 --> 00:15:16.415
It's got that —

00:15:16.415 --> 00:15:17.791
Jesus Christ.

00:15:24.006 --> 00:15:26.091
Oh, no.

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:28.010
Ooh, I don't like that.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.387
Moving on to the wasabi ranch.

00:15:30.387 --> 00:15:31.555
[sighs]

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:37.186
I'm getting very little wasabi from these.

00:15:37.186 --> 00:15:38.270
I wonder why that is.

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.189
Now, the texture of this is bizarre.

00:15:40.189 --> 00:15:41.649
It's got all these weird lumps in it.

00:15:41.649 --> 00:15:43.984
Like, what is — I don't
want that from a sauce.

00:15:43.984 --> 00:15:45.778
0.3% wasabi.

00:15:45.778 --> 00:15:48.280
So I'm assuming it's
not going to be wasabi.

00:15:53.953 --> 00:15:55.371
That's not spicy.

00:15:56.246 --> 00:15:57.539
It's just unpleasant.

00:15:59.416 --> 00:16:02.503
Chunky sauce that tastes very salty.

00:16:02.503 --> 00:16:05.005
"A versatile condiment
with a," I love this,

00:16:05.005 --> 00:16:07.257
"velvety zing."

00:16:07.257 --> 00:16:08.217
All right.

00:16:14.181 --> 00:16:15.516
Oh, s---.

00:16:16.767 --> 00:16:17.935
Oh, wow.

00:16:20.729 --> 00:16:22.731
It was velvety!

00:16:22.731 --> 00:16:24.400
And it did have a zing!

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:27.611
Hey, Kikkoman copywriters.

00:16:27.611 --> 00:16:29.488
You're doing it, guys.

00:16:29.488 --> 00:16:30.864
And then last but by no means least,

00:16:30.864 --> 00:16:33.492
we have this one, a Wasabi-O hot sauce.

00:16:39.123 --> 00:16:41.041
[coughs]

00:16:43.877 --> 00:16:45.796
Ugh, man.

00:16:45.796 --> 00:16:48.298
Ass Kickin' wasabi hot sauce.

00:16:48.298 --> 00:16:50.217
Look at that donkey.

00:16:50.217 --> 00:16:52.636
That is an ass that is kickin'.

00:16:52.636 --> 00:16:55.222
It also says habanero on here.

00:16:57.766 --> 00:16:59.143
Wish I knew that before you dumped

00:16:59.143 --> 00:17:00.561
half the bottle on the chip.

00:17:01.437 --> 00:17:02.521
Oh, man!

00:17:07.776 --> 00:17:09.069
Oh, crap.

00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.448
Ugh, man.

00:17:12.448 --> 00:17:14.116
But I like it.

00:17:14.116 --> 00:17:16.535
This goes in the Joe's Spicy Hall of Fame.

00:17:17.578 --> 00:17:19.788
[cheering]

00:17:19.788 --> 00:17:21.081
Whoa.

00:17:21.081 --> 00:17:22.791
This is a maybe. I'm not gonna —

00:17:22.791 --> 00:17:23.834
yeah, I'll put this in there.

00:17:23.834 --> 00:17:25.210
[cheering]

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:26.795
These were kind of all bad.

00:17:26.795 --> 00:17:27.963
I don't think I would eat any of these

00:17:27.963 --> 00:17:29.840
out of choice in the future.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:33.677
I'd say the wasabi mayo and the hot sauce

00:17:33.677 --> 00:17:35.721
were maybe, like, a 2 out of 5.

00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:36.972
And these ones were both, like,

00:17:36.972 --> 00:17:38.515
a 1 out of 5.

00:17:38.515 --> 00:17:40.059
How do I look? Do I look like I'm ... ?

00:17:40.059 --> 00:17:42.061
I feel like I'm losing a fight.

00:17:43.062 --> 00:17:45.022
♪ Peas and nuts ♪

00:17:45.022 --> 00:17:46.982
♪ Peas and nuts ♪

00:17:46.982 --> 00:17:49.151
♪ Gonna try a bunch of ♪

00:17:49.151 --> 00:17:50.527
♪ Peas and ♪

00:17:50.527 --> 00:17:51.945
Let's do a lightning-round-style ranking

00:17:51.945 --> 00:17:53.697
of all of these by spice.

00:17:53.697 --> 00:17:54.782
5 out of 10.

00:17:54.782 --> 00:17:55.657
1 out of 10.

00:17:56.492 --> 00:17:58.035
6 out of 10.

00:17:58.035 --> 00:17:58.869
What's that word right there?

00:17:58.869 --> 00:17:59.703
I know this is supposed
to be a lightning round.

00:17:59.703 --> 00:18:00.996
What's that word? What's that
word? Read that aloud for me.

00:18:00.996 --> 00:18:02.372
Yuelei: Hot.
Joe: Hell no.

00:18:02.372 --> 00:18:03.665
I'm gonna give that a 0.

00:18:04.792 --> 00:18:05.793
2 out of 10.

00:18:05.793 --> 00:18:06.835
Wasabi edamame.

00:18:08.295 --> 00:18:10.339
0! What is happening here?

00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:12.925
7 out of 10.

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.635
Wasabi almonds.

00:18:14.635 --> 00:18:15.719
0.5.

00:18:16.595 --> 00:18:17.429
5 out of 10.

00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:19.598
Wasabi-coated peanuts.

00:18:22.601 --> 00:18:23.727
F---.

00:18:25.938 --> 00:18:27.189
I'll give those guys an 8.

00:18:28.232 --> 00:18:29.483
2 out of 10.

00:18:29.483 --> 00:18:30.317
4 out of 10.

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:32.861
5 out of 10.

00:18:32.861 --> 00:18:33.695
3 out of 10.

00:18:34.988 --> 00:18:36.657
I'll give that a 1.

00:18:36.657 --> 00:18:39.451
I think I could easily handle
10 wasabi peas at once.

00:18:39.451 --> 00:18:40.869
10's nothing.

00:18:40.869 --> 00:18:41.703
I'll do 20.

00:18:41.703 --> 00:18:43.914
[crunching]

00:18:44.957 --> 00:18:46.792
Come on, come on, come on! Get hot!

00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:49.670
If I put 15 to 20 of
these in my mouth at once

00:18:50.629 --> 00:18:53.549
that ups the scale to, like, a 4.

00:18:53.549 --> 00:18:54.967
Here we go now.

00:18:54.967 --> 00:18:56.093
A handful.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:10.149
Oh, f---.

00:19:10.149 --> 00:19:11.608
Oh, s---.

00:19:11.608 --> 00:19:12.985
That caught me off guard.

00:19:14.695 --> 00:19:16.363
Oh, s---.

00:19:16.363 --> 00:19:19.533
I almost peed myself a
little 'cause it's so spicy.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.618
Oh, man.

00:19:23.412 --> 00:19:24.371
Now we're heading into some of the more

00:19:24.371 --> 00:19:26.373
weird and wonderful
wasabi-flavored snacks out there,

00:19:26.373 --> 00:19:28.500
and, boy, do we have some
surprising combinations.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.334
I'll start with a banger,

00:19:29.334 --> 00:19:31.170
which is wasabi cheese.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:34.756
It smells quite, quite heavily of wasabi.

00:19:34.756 --> 00:19:37.634
It's extremely rubbery,
like super plasticky,

00:19:37.634 --> 00:19:39.303
and has that very, quite threatening

00:19:39.303 --> 00:19:40.888
green wax on the outside.

00:19:44.975 --> 00:19:46.560
Yeah, that's, um.

00:19:47.728 --> 00:19:49.730
It's not for me, I don't think.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:50.689
It's just, like I said,

00:19:50.689 --> 00:19:53.859
got the texture of quite a rubbery cheese

00:19:53.859 --> 00:19:55.777
with a fairly strong wasabi aftertaste.

00:19:55.777 --> 00:19:56.945
Not really spicy.

00:19:57.905 --> 00:19:59.823
Just that kind of earthiness

00:19:59.823 --> 00:20:01.950
that you would maybe
get from actual wasabi.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.412
I too also ordered the wasabi cheese.

00:20:05.412 --> 00:20:06.663
It has not arrived.

00:20:06.663 --> 00:20:09.124
I received an email a couple days ago

00:20:09.124 --> 00:20:11.877
telling me that it's not going
to get here until February.

00:20:11.877 --> 00:20:14.129
But what I did get is this.

00:20:15.005 --> 00:20:17.132
Vegan jerky.

00:20:17.132 --> 00:20:18.342
Wasabi-flavored.

00:20:19.426 --> 00:20:21.428
I don't want this at all.

00:20:21.428 --> 00:20:24.181
Meatless jerky, we did it!

00:20:25.849 --> 00:20:26.975
[sighs]

00:20:27.935 --> 00:20:29.770
[whispering] It doesn't smell good.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:31.063
It smells — I know you can hear me

00:20:31.063 --> 00:20:32.731
'cause you have headphones on —

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.107
this smells real bad.

00:20:34.107 --> 00:20:36.526
Oh, God, I hate this.

00:20:36.526 --> 00:20:39.238
Meatless vegan jerky is terrible.

00:20:40.656 --> 00:20:43.158
And no wasabi flavor in that at all.

00:20:43.158 --> 00:20:43.992
Next up we have this one.

00:20:43.992 --> 00:20:46.620
It's Mike popcorn, and it's
wasabi-soy-sauce-flavored.

00:20:49.873 --> 00:20:52.876
My hands are so greasy from the cheese.

00:20:58.715 --> 00:21:00.217
Hm.

00:21:00.217 --> 00:21:01.260
That's actually quite pleasant.

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:02.636
That's pretty nice.

00:21:02.636 --> 00:21:04.012
Calling this the mystery bag.

00:21:04.012 --> 00:21:05.264
I saw Harry also had it.

00:21:05.264 --> 00:21:08.475
So I don't know what I
bought and what this is.

00:21:08.475 --> 00:21:11.228
Local translator Yuelei Song is saying

00:21:11.228 --> 00:21:14.898
that this is fire-flavored.

00:21:14.898 --> 00:21:16.275
Let's find out together.

00:21:16.275 --> 00:21:17.567
I don't know what this is.

00:21:25.284 --> 00:21:26.410
Uh-huh.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.244
Yep.

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:30.163
Ooh-argh!

00:21:30.163 --> 00:21:31.248
Man!

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:34.835
Aah.

00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:37.337
Yeah, it's hot.

00:21:37.337 --> 00:21:38.297
That goes in the hall of fame.

00:21:38.297 --> 00:21:40.048
[cheering]

00:21:40.048 --> 00:21:42.050
Now, these ones with this
very alarming packaging

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.218
with the big warning label

00:21:43.218 --> 00:21:46.471
are Frito-Lay Forbidden
Wasabi spicy snacks.

00:21:46.471 --> 00:21:47.681
These do kind of look like Cheetos.

00:21:47.681 --> 00:21:48.890
They also kind of look like Nik Naks,

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:51.226
which were a specific
British brand of crisps.

00:21:51.226 --> 00:21:52.185
Let's give it a try.

00:21:58.567 --> 00:21:59.526
OK.

00:22:01.903 --> 00:22:03.196
Yeah, wow.

00:22:04.781 --> 00:22:06.283
I can see why these are forbidden.

00:22:06.283 --> 00:22:08.035
That's pretty strong.

00:22:08.035 --> 00:22:09.202
Whoo!

00:22:10.245 --> 00:22:11.830
Yeah, those are good.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.206
Those are actually spicy.

00:22:13.206 --> 00:22:16.293
We're moving into the wasabi and sweets,

00:22:16.293 --> 00:22:18.086
wasabi and chocolate zone,

00:22:18.086 --> 00:22:21.840
with, first, this just
says Jackie's Chocolates.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:24.426
Jackie, if you're watching,
thank you for your chocolates.

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:28.722
Jackie, I've been eating wasabi all day,

00:22:28.722 --> 00:22:30.724
so maybe that's it, but,

00:22:30.724 --> 00:22:32.476
next to no wasabi in this.

00:22:32.476 --> 00:22:34.394
But what have I learned from before?

00:22:34.394 --> 00:22:35.729
If you can't taste the wasabi,

00:22:35.729 --> 00:22:37.773
just shove a bunch more in your mouth.

00:22:47.366 --> 00:22:48.825
Now, with slightly less alarming packaging

00:22:48.825 --> 00:22:50.452
but also supposedly very spicy,

00:22:50.452 --> 00:22:53.121
are these Raging Fire wasabi crackers.

00:22:53.121 --> 00:22:54.790
That seems like a waste of packaging.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:56.083
Lots of plastic here.

00:22:58.210 --> 00:22:59.252
Mm.

00:23:01.254 --> 00:23:03.131
[coughs]

00:23:03.131 --> 00:23:05.717
[laughs]

00:23:05.717 --> 00:23:07.219
Woo-hoo!

00:23:07.219 --> 00:23:08.178
Wow, OK.

00:23:09.096 --> 00:23:10.680
We might have a winner.

00:23:10.680 --> 00:23:12.140
We might have a 10.

00:23:13.517 --> 00:23:15.102
Those are powerful. Wow!

00:23:15.102 --> 00:23:16.937
Leon: Harry, throw it to me.

00:23:17.854 --> 00:23:20.607
[crew laughing]

00:23:20.607 --> 00:23:22.192
Hells to the yeah.

00:23:22.192 --> 00:23:23.735
Wasabi Kit Kats.

00:23:26.738 --> 00:23:28.573
I'm intrigued to see how
wasabi meshes with chocolate,

00:23:28.573 --> 00:23:29.783
so let's give it a go.

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.372
All right, go, Joe.

00:23:35.372 --> 00:23:36.915
Oh. [muffled] This is really good!

00:23:41.253 --> 00:23:43.839
Mm!

00:23:43.839 --> 00:23:45.340
I mean,

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:46.758
it's delicious.

00:23:46.758 --> 00:23:49.010
I can't quite explain why.

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.555
This might be the best-tasting thing.

00:23:51.555 --> 00:23:52.764
And of course we have this,

00:23:52.764 --> 00:23:55.225
wasabi shampoo.

00:23:55.225 --> 00:23:57.561
If you watch "Food Wars"

00:23:57.561 --> 00:23:58.812
and you thought in this episode,

00:23:58.812 --> 00:24:01.648
"Man, Joe's hair is
looking a little bit nicer.

00:24:01.648 --> 00:24:03.358
Scalp's looking a little bit healthier,

00:24:03.358 --> 00:24:04.484
a little more bounce to that guy.

00:24:04.484 --> 00:24:05.444
What's going on?"

00:24:05.444 --> 00:24:06.736
Your eyes do not deceive you.

00:24:06.736 --> 00:24:08.405
I've spent at least the last week,

00:24:08.405 --> 00:24:09.281
this long,

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:12.534
using wasabi shampoo in
this very head of hair,

00:24:12.534 --> 00:24:14.327
and I gotta say, it's pretty nice.

00:24:15.203 --> 00:24:18.165
Doesn't really smell
wasabi-like, but yeah.

00:24:18.165 --> 00:24:19.082
I honestly have no idea

00:24:19.082 --> 00:24:21.251
how to incorporate this
into the video, but,

00:24:21.251 --> 00:24:24.588
there was a film called
"Wasabi" starring Jean Reno,

00:24:24.588 --> 00:24:26.506
and I just thought it
was worth mentioning.

00:24:26.506 --> 00:24:27.632
Yeah, I got it too.

00:24:27.632 --> 00:24:29.134
"Wasabi," the movie.

00:24:30.135 --> 00:24:31.678
I don't know anything about it.

00:24:33.722 --> 00:24:35.015
I haven't seen it.

00:24:36.892 --> 00:24:38.226
I don't know what else to say.

00:24:40.770 --> 00:24:42.230
That means it's time to
talk about the second reason

00:24:42.230 --> 00:24:44.232
as to why all your wasabi is fake.

00:24:46.485 --> 00:24:47.611
So, yeah, in just 30 minutes,

00:24:47.611 --> 00:24:48.945
our wasabi has gone from that lovely

00:24:48.945 --> 00:24:51.072
vibrant green paste to this.

00:24:51.072 --> 00:24:52.741
It's kind of a slightly sad-looking

00:24:52.741 --> 00:24:56.036
yellow and brown crusty little blob.

00:24:56.036 --> 00:24:58.872
And it has almost no odor.

00:24:58.872 --> 00:24:59.873
That's really weird.

00:25:03.627 --> 00:25:05.754
Nope, nothing.

00:25:05.754 --> 00:25:07.464
That's wild.

00:25:07.464 --> 00:25:09.799
There's so little, little
flavor to that. Wow.

00:25:12.385 --> 00:25:13.678
Wow, it's flavorless.

00:25:15.639 --> 00:25:18.058
Like, it's not even kind of wasabi-ish.

00:25:18.058 --> 00:25:20.685
Completely flavorless. Wow.

00:25:20.685 --> 00:25:22.479
There are a couple of ways
around this volatility,

00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:23.813
like how some of the powders from earlier

00:25:23.813 --> 00:25:25.690
were freeze-dried to preserve the flavor.

00:25:25.690 --> 00:25:26.566
But if you're at a restaurant,

00:25:26.566 --> 00:25:28.193
unless you're seeing
a rhizome being grated

00:25:28.193 --> 00:25:29.027
right in front of you,

00:25:29.027 --> 00:25:31.321
you're probably eating fake wasabi.

00:25:31.321 --> 00:25:34.115
I am sick of wasabi. Are we done yet?

00:25:34.115 --> 00:25:34.950
Not yet, Joe.

00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:36.826
We've got one more surprise
up our sleeves for you.

00:25:39.454 --> 00:25:41.540
Oh, OK. Back in a second.

00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:44.125
[cheering]

00:25:46.586 --> 00:25:47.712
Cool.

00:25:53.051 --> 00:25:54.135
Is that too much?

00:25:54.135 --> 00:25:56.513
Charlie: Uh ... we'll see.

00:26:02.811 --> 00:26:04.437
I'm back. The crew has set this up.

00:26:04.437 --> 00:26:06.439
I know very little about
what is in any of these.

00:26:06.439 --> 00:26:07.440
I'm assuming some kind of

00:26:07.440 --> 00:26:08.984
wasabi-based surprise is in one of them,

00:26:08.984 --> 00:26:10.110
but we're going to find out.

00:26:10.110 --> 00:26:11.236
I'm going to pick one and eat it.

00:26:11.236 --> 00:26:12.070
Wish me luck.

00:26:14.906 --> 00:26:16.199
Oh, spicy.

00:26:22.539 --> 00:26:24.666
[mumbling]

00:26:27.252 --> 00:26:28.795
Ugh.

00:26:28.795 --> 00:26:30.213
Oh!

00:26:30.213 --> 00:26:31.047
Oh!

00:26:33.008 --> 00:26:34.342
F---.

00:26:39.639 --> 00:26:40.473
Oh!

00:26:42.309 --> 00:26:44.811
Oh, my God, it's so bad.

00:26:47.397 --> 00:26:48.231
Ugh.

00:26:54.821 --> 00:26:56.072
Oh, f---.

00:26:57.324 --> 00:26:58.742
Oh, my God.

00:26:58.742 --> 00:26:59.576
Ugh.

00:27:01.745 --> 00:27:02.996
Thanks for watching. If you enjoyed this,

00:27:02.996 --> 00:27:04.664
check out our "Fast
Food Chemistry" episode

00:27:04.664 --> 00:27:07.417
where I made popcorn chicken
using 42 ingredients.

